<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shravasti</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Savatthi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shravasti, in Pali Savatthi, was the capital of the kingdom of Kosala in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and one of the largest cities of the Buddha's time. The Buddha spent many rainy seasons at its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jetavana">Jetavana</a> monastery, and Jain tradition makes it the birthplace of the tirthankara Sambhavanatha. Its ruins, at Sahet-Mahet near the Rapti River in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttar-pradesh">Uttar Pradesh</a>, are a major Buddhist pilgrimage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shravasti.jpg" alt="Shravasti" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varun Shiv Kapur from New Delhi, India · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shobhnath_temple_(5703067291)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
